  "notes": "Bhutan counts Class PP (pre-primary) as the first of seven primary years (PP–VI); like other pre-primary years it is left out here, so Class I is year 1. The Statistical Yearbook of Bhutan 2025 cited here gives primary PP–VI, lower secondary VII–VIII, middle IX–X and higher secondary XI–XII, with 5 as the official age for PP, so Class I starts at 6. News reports say the National Education Policy 2025 set PP entry at 6 from 2026 and the Cabinet then kept it at 5; neither official text could be fetched."
